#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Setup instructions for IBM Quantum on IBM Cloud to submit Qiskit SDK and IBM"
" Quantum Compute Service jobs for users without email invitations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up your IBM Cloud account"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore urlendcoded, WQVY */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set up your IBM Cloud account {#set-up-your-ibm-cloud-account}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you were emailed an invitation to join an account, follow the steps in "
"[Set up your IBM Cloud account - invited users](/guides/cloud-setup-invited)"
" instead.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can run workloads on IBM&reg; quantum processing units (QPUs) by setting"
" up an account on IBM Cloud&reg;. You will also need to [install and set up "
"Qiskit and the IBM Quantum Compute client](/guides/install-qiskit#local).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Your user account is associated with one or more "
"[instances](/guides/instances) identified by _Cloud Resource Names_ (CRNs) "
"that give access to IBM Quantum services. Additionally, a unique API token "
"(also called a key) is assigned to each account, allowing for IBM Quantum "
"access from Qiskit.  For instructions to choose a specific instance, see "
"[Connect to an instance](./instances#connect-instance).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"cloud\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set up to use IBM Cloud {#set-up-to-use-ibm-cloud}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin {#before-you-begin}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you do not already have one, set up an [IBM Cloud account](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/registration).\n"
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"You can be part of multiple IBM Cloud accounts.  You can access any of your IBM Cloud accounts at any time from the account switcher in the header of the [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com) interface.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Log in to [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com) with an "
"IBMid or Google account.  If you don't have one, you are guided through "
"creating one. (These login credentials are not your IBM Cloud account "
"credentials.)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Make sure that the correct account and region are selected in the account "
"switcher in the header, as shown in the following image.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    The region controls where your jobs are run and where the job data is "
"kept. You can access either region by using the same API key, but you can "
"only see and access the instances that were created in the region that "
"you're logged in to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ![The IBM Quantum Platform header is shown.  The account switcher is to "
"the right of the search bar.  The region switcher is to the right of the "
"account switcher.](/docs/images/guides/cloud-setup/IQP-Header.avif 'IBM "
"Quantum Platform header')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Create an instance {#1-create-an-instance}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can create an instance from the IBM Quantum Platform "
"[Instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances) page.  See [Create an "
"instance](/guides/instances#add-instance) for detailed instructions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2. Optional: Save your access credentials {#2-optional-save-your-access-"
"credentials}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are using a trusted Python environment, such as a personal laptop, it"
" is recommended that you use the `save_account()` method to [save your "
"credentials locally](/guides/save-credentials).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"cloud-save\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3. Connect Qiskit with your service instance {#3-connect-qiskit-with-your-"
"service-instance}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Initialize the service](/guides/initialize-account) in a **trusted Python "
"environment**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Initialize the service in an **untrusted environment**](/guides/cloud-"
"setup-untrusted) (such as a public computer)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Notes\">\n"
"   * Follow [these instructions](/guides/cloud-setup-rest-api) if you want to connect by using the REST API instead of using Qiskit.\n"
"   * If necessary, use [this information](/guides/quickstart-steps-org#firewall) to configure your firewall to enable access to the IBM Quantum API endpoints.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"  -  [Overview of available plans](plans-overview).\n"
"  -  [Configure the Qiskit SDK locally](configure-qiskit-local).\n"
"  -  [View your available QPUs](/guides/qpu-information#available).\n"
"  -  Follow the steps in the [Run your first circuit on hardware](/guides/hello-world) guide to write and run a quantum program.\n"
"  -  [Set up to use IBM Quantum Platform with REST API](/guides/cloud-setup-rest-api).\n"
"  -  Try a [tutorial](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/tutorials).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
